          "text": "You are an expert TikTok creative strategist. Your task is to reverse-engineer a viral TikTok video into a fully structured script and frame-by-frame storyboard.\n\nWatch the entire video carefully. Identify every creative decision — format, hook style, section structure, selling approach, pacing, and visual execution. Capture the exact spoken words and describe every frame.\n\nTAXONOMY REFERENCE:\n\nSECTIONS AND SECTION DETAILS:\n- Hook: Pattern interrupt / Scroll-stopper, Big promise / Bold claim, Audience call-out, Credibility snap, Outcome preview\n- On-ramp: Problem-in-one-line, Outcome-in-one-line, Audience call-out + promise, Pattern-break context, Curiosity frame, Why listen to me, Mini-story setup, Time/effort reframe, What you will get from watching, Social proof baked in\n- Problem: Problem statement, Stakes / consequences, Empathy moment\n- Agitation: Agitation / dramatization, Desire / transformation vision\n- Motivator: Desire, Transformation, Proof, Social proof, Identity\n- Solution Intro: Discovery moment, Unique mechanism, Positioning / comparison\n- Product Intro: Product reveal, Feature snapshot, Discovery moment, Unique mechanism, Positioning / comparison\n- Demonstration: Demo / show don't tell, Before / after, Mini tutorial / how-to, Use-case montage, Feature deep-dive, What is included\n- Education: Explainer, Myth-busting, Ingredient / science breakdown, Mini tutorial / how-to, Before / after\n- Proof: Personal testimonial, Metrics / data proof, Third-party testimonials\n- Trust Builder: Social proof, Authority / credentials, Third-party testimonials, Metrics / data proof, Objection handling, Risk reversal\n- Objections: Objection handling, Risk reversal, Empathy moment, Social proof, Metrics / data proof\n- Reassurances: Post-CTA reassurance, Risk reversal, Simple recap\n- Offer Stack: Core offer statement, Value stacking, Bonus section, Price justification\n- Persuasion Levers: Scarcity / urgency, Segment-specific benefit recap, Identity / values alignment\n- Engagement: Engagement ask, Identity / values alignment\n- Community: Community invitation\n- Call To Action: Primary CTA, Micro-CTA, Simple recap\n- Urgency: Reason to act now, Deadline / expiring bonus, Scarcity / urgency\n- Outro: Post-CTA reassurance, Brand tag, Simple recap\n\nSHOT TYPES (use exactly as written):\nFace-to-Camera, Talking Head, Interview Style, Single, Two-Shot, B-Roll, C-Roll, Cutaway, Reaction Shot, Extreme Wide Shot, Wide/Long Shot, Full Shot, Medium Long Shot, Cowboy Shot, Medium Shot, Medium Close-Up, Close-Up, Extreme Close-Up, Over-the-Shoulder, Pan, Tilt, Tracking/Following, Handheld/Walk-and-Talk, Dutch Angle, Low Angle, High Angle, Product Shot, Before/After Split, Screen Recording, Text Overlay Shot, Transition Shot\n\nVOICEOVER HOOK TYPES — for the Hook frame only:\nPain / Problem, Contrarian, Statistics / Numbers, Enemy / Comparison, Before / After, Social Proof, Direct Question, Pattern Interrupt, Desired Outcome, Curiosity Gap, Call Out, Confession / Vulnerability, Authority / Credibility, Story Setup, Urgency / Scarcity, Relatability, Challenge / Dare, Revelation / Secret\n\nCAPTION HOOK TYPES — for the Hook frame only:\nPOV Scenarios, Question Hooks, Gifting Hooks, Authority Building, Social Proof, PSA / Announcement, Urgency / Time-Sensitive, Shock / Surprise, Numbers / Statistics, Scenario / Story, Surprise Reveals, Benefit Showcase, Problem Identification, Routine Showcase, Sales & Promotion, Enemy\n\nVISUAL ACTION HOOK TYPES — for the Hook frame only:\nNative Interaction, Yapping, Problem, Stitch, Product Reveal, Demo / Application, Pattern Interrupt, Lifestyle / POV, Transformation, Reaction, Unboxing, Text Overlay\n\nFORMAT OPTIONS (identify which one this video uses):\nUs Versus Them, Feature Point Out, Founder, Expert Explainer, Post-it, Before and After, Native Text Overlay, Skit / Comedy Skit, Press, Testimonial / Customer Review, Storytelling, Greenscreen, Tutorial, Social Proof