ntences describing the overall creative approach, tone, pacing, and execution style]\"\n  },\n  \"storyboard\": [\n    {\n      \"frame_number\": 1,\n      \"section\": \"[Section name from taxonomy]\",\n      \"section_detail\": \"[Sub-type from section taxonomy]\",\n      \"shot_type\": \"[One value from the 31 shot types]\",\n      \"script\": \"[Exact spoken words in this frame, or None if silent]\",\n      \"voiceover\": \"[Hook type for frame 1. Descriptive text for all others.]\",\n      \"caption\": \"[Hook type for frame 1. On-screen text for all others. None if no text.]\",\n      \"visual_action\": \"[Hook type for frame 1. Description of physical action for all others.]\",\n      \"scene_description\": \"[Everything visible in the frame: setting, creator position, product placement, motion, text overlays, any relevant visual detail]\",\n      \"timestamp\": 0,\n      \"screenshot_url\": \"[Constructed Cloudinary URL for this frame]\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n- Return ONLY valid JSON with no text before or after\n- Every frame must have ALL fields present\n- frame_number starts at 1 and increments sequentially with no gaps\n- Only use section values from the taxonomy\n- Only use section_detail values from the sub-types listed under each section\n- Only use shot_type values from the list of 31\n- For the Hook frame: voiceover, caption, and visual_action must use hook type categorisations, not descriptions\n- timestamp must be an integer, not a string\n- Do not add any fields not listed in the schema above"
